From 69d95330b94ba9bf7a6dbe9e9f2d47f8d5b35471 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeongkyu Shin <jshin@lablup.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:50:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rocm): implement FFT through hipFFT

FFT was a NO_GPU stub. fft.hip ports mlx/backend/cuda/fft.cu, keeping its axis walk, the packing of the transform axis to the back and the inverse scaling, with two differences. hipFFT has no hipfftXtMakePlanMany or hipfftXtExec, so the typed API is used instead: one hipfftType (C2C, R2C or C2R) per plan and one exec function per transform, which is enough because MLX only asks for float32 and complex64 here. And hipFFT work cannot be a HIP graph kernel node, so execution goes through CommandEncoder::launch_kernel, the path the rocBLAS and hipBLASLt GEMMs take. hipfft joins the link list, with a configure-time error when it is missing.

The plan cache holds 128 entries, as in the CUDA file. It depends on the blocking-sync flag being set before the first HIP queue exists ("fix(rocm): set blocking-sync before the first HIP queue is created", which has to land first): without that, the first plan eviction past about 16 live plans hangs inside hipfftDestroy.

MLX_ROCM_FFT_CACHE_SIZE overrides the capacity. The LRU cache read it with an unchecked std::stoul: "0" was accepted and the first put() then popped an empty list (undefined behavior), "-1" became SIZE_MAX, "8abc" became 8, and anything else threw a bare "stoul" out of a static initializer, so every later FFT threw again. capacity_from_env() now takes a whole decimal integer from 1 to INT_MAX; anything else prints one line to stderr and uses the default. LRUCache and LRUBytesKeyCache throw for a capacity of 0, as the CUDA LRUCache does.

Verified against the CPU stream for rfft, irfft, round trips and complex fft at lengths 2, 8, 400, 512, 1024, 1200 and 2048 and batches up to 512, all within 1e-5 relative.
